  {
    "description": "Start here. Then describeNodeTypes for any node type you'll add.
The whole workflow as a compact outline: the trigger, then one line per step (ID, type, name, short config), sections (▣) and notes, nested by branch, with issue counts. A big workflow is cut to fit budget (characters, default 4000): omitted lists what was left out, each with the exact call (tool and args) that fetches it.
Example: {}",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "budget": {
          "description": "Size limit in characters of the result",
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "overview",
  },
  {
    "description": "Part of the workflow in overview's format: one step's subtree (stepId), one of its branches (stepId and branch) or the top-level list (neither). after pages a list: only the steps after that step. Use it, or the calls in omitted, to expand what overview collapsed.
Example: {"stepId":"<stepId>","branch":"if"}",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$defs": {
        "Branch": {
          "description": "A branch ID. The valid IDs depend on the node: see branches in describeNodeTypes",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "after": {
          "type": "string",
        },
        "branch": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Branch",
        },
        "budget": {
          "description": "Size limit in characters of the result",
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "stepId": {
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "outline",
  },
  {
    "description": "Everything needed to edit one step: config, its compact input schema, the refs in scope, issues, branches, its note and its section (section: title, colour and note; heads: other sections that start here, with their notes).
Strings over 500 chars are cut, ending in a fixed marker "…(+N chars)" that is not part of the value; the step's cut lists the cut paths, and full is the call that returns them uncut.
Over budget (characters, default 8000), refs and then the schema are left out, each listed in omitted with its call.
Example: {"stepId":"<stepId>"}",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "budget": {
          "description": "Size limit in characters of the result",
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "full": {
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "stepId": {
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "stepId",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "focus",
  },
  {
    "description": "Several steps in focus's detail: pass exactly one of ids or where (a selector, paged with after and limit: default 50, at most 200). include picks the extras: "config" (the default), "schema", "refs". Unknown IDs are in missing.
Only the leading steps that fit budget (characters, default 8000) are returned; next is the call for more and remaining counts the steps left: follow next until remaining is 0; if next.ids is a slice, re-request the rest of your list.
Strings over 500 chars are cut, ending in a fixed marker "…(+N chars)" that is not part of the value; the step's cut lists the cut paths, and full is the call that returns them uncut. Here full is one call for every cut step of the page.
Example: {"ids":["<stepId>","<otherStepId>"],"include":["config"]}",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$defs": {
        "Branch": {
          "description": "A branch ID. The valid IDs depend on the node: see branches in describeNodeTypes",
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "NodeType": {
          "description": "A node type of this app (describeNodeTypes gives its config)",
          "enum": [
            "core.condition",
            "core.switch",
            "core.forEach",
            "core.stop",
            "core.delay",
            "core.waitForCallback",
            "core.callSubflow",
            "core.httpRequest",
            "core.transform",
            "crm.findContactByEmail",
            "crm.getContact",
            "crm.createContact",
            "crm.updateContact",
            "crm.assignOwner",
            "crm.getDeal",
            "crm.updateDeal",
            "crm.getUser",
            "crm.sendEmail",
            "crm.requestApproval",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "Where": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "description": "A step selector; fields are ANDed and {} matches every step. within: descendants of a step (optionally of one branch); section: a section's steps; configHas: a config path that is set.",
          "properties": {
            "configHas": {
              "type": "string",
            },
            "nameContains": {
              "type": "string",
            },
            "section": {
              "type": "string",
            },
            "type": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/NodeType",
            },
            "within": {
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "properties": {
                "branch": {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/Branch",
                },
                "stepId": {
                  "minLength": 1,
                  "type": "string",
                },
              },
              "required": [
                "stepId",
              ],
              "type": "object",
            },
          },
          "type": "object",
        },
      },
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Pass exactly one of ids or where; after and limit page a where selector.",
      "properties": {
        "after": {
          "type": "string",
        },
        "budget": {
          "description": "Size limit in characters of the result",
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "full": {
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "ids": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string",
          },
          "type": "array",
        },
        "include": {
          "description": "Extras per step: "config" (the default), "schema", "refs"",
          "items": {
            "enum": [
              "config",
              "schema",
              "refs",
            ],
            "type": "string",
          },
          "type": "array",
        },
        "limit": {
          "description": "Page size",
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "where": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Where",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "getSteps",
  },
  {
    "description": "The IDs and outline lines of the steps a where selector matches (fields ANDed; {} matches all), and count, the number of matches. Pages of limit (default 100, at most 500) after the step after; omitted has the call for the next page. Check a selector here before a command with where and expect.
Example: {"where":{"type":"crm.findContactByEmail"}}",
